            <ArticleTitle>Capitate-hamate fusion for Kienböck's disease. Good results in 8 cases followed for 3 years.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>560-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>8 patients with Kienböck's disease and without negative ulnar variance were treated with a modification of Chuinard's capitate-hamate fusion. All patients returned to their normal activities free of pain. The postoperative wrist motion was unchanged, but the grip strength was increased.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
